+### 36.4. Supplied structure and affected-source limits
+
+All four supplied Documentation components have README.md and 01-Architecture/02-Structure/03-Behavior/04-Reference directories. Their actual Markdown counts by those categories are Metadata 4/4/4/3, Document Identity 4/3/4/4, Classification 3/3/5/4 and Templates 3/3/5/4. This is presence evidence, not conformity of their meanings, headers, maps or implementation. Reviews is an added partial set with only Behavior/Reference documentation; README and the other two directories are not supplied. The proposed contract must expose that incomplete coverage, without manufacturing missing documents or introducing an unstated exception.
+
+Metadata Dictionary §§1–3/6–7 defines canonical Metadata Element semantics and entry organization, while Schema §§1–3 excludes element semantics. The received Metadata README still maps Dictionary to Reference although its actual path is 02-Structure. Document Identity's README Structure map includes Elements while the actual supplied file resides in Architecture. Templates README shows illustrative direct component filenames rather than the supplied category paths. These remain consumer-map reconciliation, not permission to force title-based classification or silently move files.
+
+Classification Lifecycle §§1–3 governs classification definitions and distinguishes document lifecycle. Metadata Specification §4 explicitly incorporates supporting sources normatively. The documentation organization standard must preserve these domain contracts without taking over their semantics, treating every lifecycle as Workflow or making only specifications normative.
+
+The actual Roadmaps/ root contains RDM-001 and component roadmaps RDM-010/020/030/040 under their received Documentation component directories. RDM-001 §§4–5 separates planning from architectural Layers and shows that root. No docs/06-Roadmaps/ path is supplied. Central storage does not change component roadmap Family/Type, allocate new identities or prove an implemented planning system.
